Recommends: pyra-hacks (>= 0.38+pyra3),
            pyra-backlight (>= 0.4)
Description: settings only the DragonBox Pyra has
 Pyra Settings is a small GTK 3 app for the Pyra's own settings: which
 buttons and whether the lid wake the machine from suspend, what the lid and
 a critical battery do, what the nubs do, how the volume wheel maps to
 speaker and headphone volume, how far the screen dims when idle and the
 keyboard light level at login.
 .
 Root-only settings go through a pkexec helper that writes only known files.
 Wake settings are kept in /etc/pyra-settings/pyra-settings.conf, which
 pyra-settings-apply.service reapplies at boot. The Volume wheel page needs
 the pyra-hacks fork and the Display & keyboard light page needs
 pyra-backlight.
